1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:01,800
So a brother in the comments asked me,

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:04,560
how can we bring softness into a relationship?

3
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:06,560
Contrary to the triggered men in my comments,

4
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:09,200
I believe softness is not about feminine or masculine.

5
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,900
It's about how you show up.

6
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:14,660
Softness is the difference between showing up amenable

7
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:16,400
and showing up oppositional.

8
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:18,320
Now amenable is a word that can get a bad rap

9
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,840
at a certain point because what it means in the beginning

10
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,240
is someone who is willing to be responsive,

11
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:25,400
willing to listen, willing to compromise.

12
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:26,680
But it can go too far past that

13
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:29,240
to where people expect that person to be submissive.

14
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:30,640
So that's when people feel like

15
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:32,840
that's softness, that's weakness.

16
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:34,300
But then there's oppositional.

17
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:36,700
And oppositional is confrontational for no reason

18
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:38,320
other than simply to defend.

19
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:39,780
And often in our partnerships,

20
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:42,880
both parties are showing up way more oppositional

21
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:44,820
and not enough amenable.

22
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:47,740
The softness comes in everybody creating a space

23
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:49,260
where we can all be amenable

24
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:51,640
because we don't feel like we gotta be oppositional

25
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,620
because we didn't come here to fight.

26
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:55,000
We came here to love.

27
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,260
Ba-dum-bum.

28
00:00:56,260 --> 00:00:58,620
For more on this, check out my Small Doses podcast episode,

29
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:00,020
Side Effects of Softness.

